msgstr "{} kolliderer fortsatt"

#. error banner: an artifact the user had open is gone; {} is "This artifact" or its quoted title
msgid "{} was deleted on the Host"
msgstr "{} ble slettet på Hosten"

#. warning above the composer: the backend's workspace has no credits left; {} is the backend's name (Codex, Claude)
msgid "{} workspace is out of credits"
msgstr "Arbeidsområdet hos {} er tomt for kreditt"

#. agent profile, Backend picker title on the model step; {} is the backend's name ("Claude · Model")
msgid "{} · Model"
msgstr "{} · Modell"

#. Settings > Kept processes, a fixed limit's value while limits are on Auto; {} is the value; changing it switches the limits to Fixed
msgid "{} · fixed limit, setting it switches to fixed"
msgstr "{} · fast grense, endring bytter til Fast"

#. Queued messages dialog, subtitle under the title when the queue is paused; {} is the chat's name
msgid "{} · paused"
msgstr "{} · satt på pause"

#. Settings, a percentage value; {} is the number
msgid "{}%"
msgstr "{} %"

#. key-binding editor, error when the key belongs to another action; {} is "<key> already runs <action> in <context>"; Enter and Esc are keys
msgid "{}. Enter takes it over, Esc keeps it there."
msgstr "{}. Enter tar den over, Esc lar den være der."

#. form card, chart's spoken summary (accessibility): a data series' name before its points; {} is the name
msgid "{}: "
msgstr "{}: "

#. Ctrl+K, placeholder while a setting's options are listed; {} is the setting's name
msgid "{}: choose one"
msgstr "{}: velg ett"

#. Settings > Import settings…, a problem with the imported file, listed on the settings page; {} is the problem (one of the "must be" lines); that value was not applied
msgid "{}; skipped"
msgstr "{}; hoppet over"

#. Settings, a size relative to normal; {} is the number, × means times
msgid "{}×"
msgstr "{}×"

#. voice picker dialog, title; {} is the agent's name (the dialog picks the voice the agent speaks with)
msgid "{}’s voice"
msgstr "Stemmen til {}"

#. chat header, how long until the agent is back; {} is a number of minutes (about)
msgid "~{} min"
msgstr "~{} min"

#. chat header, how long until the agent is back; {} is a number of seconds (about)
msgid "~{} s"
msgstr "~{} s"

#. error banner, the artifact meant when it has no title; or its title in quotation marks (use the language's own quotation marks)
msgid "“{}”"
msgstr "«{}»"

#. chat, wide table, clickable hint above it once scrolled to the end: scrolls back to the first columns; the arrow points left
msgid "← back to the start"
msgstr "← tilbake til starten"

#. process output view, line under the log while scrolled up; {n} is how many lines the view is above the newest; "End" is the keyboard key that jumps back to the newest line (keep the key name as the key is labelled)
msgid "↑ {n} line back · End for the latest"
msgid_plural "↑ {n} lines back · End for the latest"
msgstr[0] "↑ {n} linje tilbake · End for nyeste"
msgstr[1] "↑ {n} linjer tilbake · End for nyeste"

#. Settings > Keyboard, the keys that move around the settings page; key names stay as they are, "search" and "default" say what / and Delete do
msgid "↑↓ / Tab · Home / End · / search · Delete default"
msgstr "↑↓ / Tab · Home / End · / søk · Delete standard"

#. Settings page, key help beside the title; the arrows, Enter, −+, ⌫, ⇧⌫, / and Esc are keys left as is; each word says what its key does (move, change, adjust, reset, reset the section, search, go back: verbs, "section" short for reset the section)
msgid ""
"↑↓ move · Enter change · ←→ / −+ adjust · ⌫ reset · ⇧⌫ section · / search · Esc back"
msgstr ""
"↑↓ flytt · Enter endre · ←→ / −+ juster · ⌫ tilbakestill · ⇧⌫ seksjon · / søk · Esc tilbake"

#. Ctrl+K, the key hint line while a setting's options are listed; key names stay, the words say what each key does
msgid "↑↓ move · Enter chooses · Esc back to everything"
msgstr "↑↓ flytt · Enter velger · Esc tilbake til alt"

#. Ctrl+R recent agents list, the key hint line at the bottom; key names stay, the words say what each key does (verbs)
#. contact picker, hint line: arrows move, Enter opens, Esc closes (keys stay as they are)
msgid "↑↓ move · Enter open · Esc close"
msgstr "↑↓ flytt · Enter åpne · Esc lukk"

#. quick switcher, key help under the list; ↑↓, Enter and Esc are key names left as is; move/run/switch/close are verbs
msgid "↑↓ move · Enter run or switch · Esc close"
msgstr "↑↓ flytt · Enter kjør eller bytt · Esc lukk"

#. Ctrl+K command palette, the key hint line at the bottom; key names stay, the words say what each key does
msgid ""
"↑↓ move · Enter runs a command, switches a setting or lists its choices · Esc close"
msgstr "↑↓ bla · Enter kjør, bytt eller vis valg · Esc lukk"

#. chat, wide table, clickable hint above it: scrolls the table sideways to its end; {n} is how many columns it has; the arrow points right
msgid "→ {n} column"
msgid_plural "→ {n} columns"
msgstr[0] "→ {n} kolonne"
msgstr[1] "→ {n} kolonner"

#. Settings page, key help beside the title while the search field has focus; ↓, Enter and Esc are key names left as is; "results" means go to the results, "clear" empties the search (verb)
msgid "↓ / Enter results · Esc clear"
msgstr "↓ / Enter resultater · Esc tøm"

#. composer, notice above the editor while voice is recorded; the dot stays; Ctrl+Shift+Space is a key name and stays untranslated; "sends" means pressing it sends the recording
msgid "● Recording · Ctrl+Shift+Space sends"
msgstr "● Tar opp · Ctrl+Shift+Space sender"

